# Line endings are pinned here rather than left to each contributor's
# core.autocrlf, which is a machine-level setting installed by Git for Windows.
# CI runs on ubuntu-latest, windows-latest and macos-latest, so checkouts need
# to be byte-identical regardless of who cloned and how their Git was set up.
#
# text=auto  -> detect text vs binary, store LF in the repository
# eol=lf     -> check out LF on every platform, Windows included
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary

# Notebooks are JSON, so they are text — but the diffs are unreadable noise
# and outputs are stripped before committing anyway (see CONTRIBUTING.md).
*.ipynb text eol=lf
